# Backend Platform SDK — Project Rules (Index)

This repository uses **Cursor rules** under `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` for maintainable, scoped guidance.

Keep this file short; add new/updated rules as separate `.mdc` files.

## Core principles (always on)

- This is a **Kotlin/Ktor backend library (SDK)** — not a standalone app. Avoid hardcoded app assumptions; prefer configuration (env + DI) and optional features.
- **FQN in Kotlin code is forbidden**: do not write fully qualified names in expressions/type annotations/generics; use imports (or typealias). Only keep minimal FQN when imports are impossible/ambiguous, and explain the reason in PR/commit message.
- **Do not run tests** after writing/editing tests, and do not suggest running them. Write correct, runnable test code; execution is up to the user.

## Detailed rules live in `.cursor/rules/`

- `project-overview.mdc` — project identity, stack, repo/module layout, boundaries.
- `architecture-patterns.mdc` — routing/bootstrap/config/layering conventions.
- `docs-kdoc-basics.mdc` + `docs-kdoc-type-requirements.mdc` — **mandatory** KDoc and documentation rules.
- `localization.mdc` — localization resource layout and naming.
- `testing-style.mdc` — JUnit/MockK conventions, placement, scope, and Gradle test deps.
- `ai-workflow.mdc` — dependency changes, routing guidance, and SDK vs sample boundaries.
